      "report": {
        "schema_version": "m0-report-v2",
        "assessment_status": "completed",
        "conclusion": "partial",
        "summary": "The alert reproduces: the 5-minute error ratio for checkout's otel-demo.CheckoutService/PlaceOrder SERVER spans rises 0 -> 0.5 (09:48:24Z) -> 0.667 -> 1.0 (from 09:50:24Z through 09:51:54Z), matching the firing time. However the denominator is tiny: over the hour ending 09:52:03Z there are only 77.29 PlaceOrder server spans in total (3.05 STATUS_CODE_ERROR, 74.24 STATUS_CODE_UNSET), so '100%' rests on ~3-4 spans per 5-minute window, and the same series shows the untagged-span rate falling to 0 while the error rate is only ~0.0125/s. The failures are not random: checkout's only failing downstream call is oteldemo.PaymentService/Charge (client span, rpc.grpc.status_code=2), whose child is payment's grpc.oteldemo.PaymentService/Charge server span throwing 'Payment request failed. Invalid token. app.loyalty.level=gold' at charge.js:37, and all other checkout dependencies (cart, currency, product-catalog, shipping) returned gRPC status 0 in the sampled traces. Payment's Charge error rate is 0 for every window from 08:22:03Z up to the window ending 09:49:03Z and then appears, with no successful Charge spans in the most recent 5-minute window; checkout-facing traffic from the frontend continued at its prior rate, so this is an application-level rejection inside payment rather than checkout or payment becoming unreachable. Root cause (what changed in payment at ~09:48Z: config, feature flag, deployment, or bad request data) is not observable with the permitted tools, so the conclusion is partial."
      }
    }
  },
